                        towards right.</p><q type="pressmark">B.lxx.</q></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">A note by John Russell, s. xviii, on fol. 1v
                     reads 'This book was written &amp; possessed by Broughtone afterwards it
                     belonged to Champeneye afterwards to William Barbone as appears by this Rime O
                     Deus Anselmi Barbone miserere Wylelmi'. This is therefore the manuscript once
                     at St Andrew's, Norwich (cf. Parochial Libraries of the Church of England, p.
                     93). 'O deus ... Willelmi' is also in Cambridge, Gonville &amp; Caius, 330,
                     along with the note 'Galfridus Champeneys'.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Armorial bookplate of Edward Roger Murray
                     Pratt, Ryston Hall (Norfolk). Sold 27 July 1925, lot 67.</provenance>
